    {
      "strength": "STRONG",
      "observation": "The two historical-memory arms matched the stock P0 trajectories through E10 in all ten seed/dataset groups. No selected like-for-like C3−C2 comparison meets +.001, and no readout/dataset pair passes both registered contrasts and the six-cell guard. MovieLens C3−C2 selected intervals exclude a +.001 gain on both readouts."
    },
    {
      "strength": "STRONG",
      "observation": "At E50 on MovieLens and KuaiRand, fixed-EMA C2 and C3 both improve AUC against continued current pairwise in all five seeds, with much smaller selected effects. Both KuaiRand fixed-EMA memories improve same-checkpoint selected LL over C1 across all five seeds. The random-history comparator shares these effects, and the results do not support added selected ranking benefits from correctness filtering."
    },
    {
      "strength": "MEDIUM",
      "observation": "KuaiRand fixed EMA C3−C1 improves both largest-domain d1 tasks and both smallest-domain d2 tasks, while both middle-sized d0 tasks decline and d0t1 falls by about .0221. Traffic/Pooled improve despite the failed guard. The A1 clean-pair comparison showed the opposite d0/d1 pattern; domain size alone cannot explain either."
    },
    {
      "strength": "WEAK",
      "observation": "Generic replay, reduced push from soft teacher targets, and shifts in selected epoch are competing explanations. C3’s LL effect against C2 is modest and one KuaiRand fixed-EMA interval barely excludes zero. A future matched soft-versus-hard comparison could isolate this contribution given an independently justified signal; C4 does not run under the registered gate."
    }
  ]
